# Docs code snippets

## Always show a path

Every fenced example that belongs in an app file must include a Starlight `title` path (arbitrary but realistic):

````markdown
```python title="app/providers/orbit_panel_provider.py"
Panel.make("admin")
    .path("admin")
    .brand_name("Acme")
```
````

Use `title="terminal"` for shell commands. Do not leave path-less Python fences.

## No wrapping parentheses

Do **not** wrap fluent chains in assignment parentheses.

```python
# ❌ BAD
panel = (
    Panel.make("admin")
    .path("admin")
)

# ❌ BAD (invalid Python — assignment + indented continuation)
panel = Panel.make("admin")
    .path("admin")

# ✅ GOOD — expression fragment (docs convention, matches forms pages)
Panel.make("admin")
    .path("admin")
    .brand_name("Acme")
```

When you need a real assignment in a full class/method example, keep the chain on one line. Prefer expression fragments for fluent demos.

Keep real call parentheses on methods that take arguments (`.path("admin")`, `.email()`).

## API tables

List method names **without** filler `()` / `(...)` — e.g. `.dark_mode`, `.path` — and describe arguments in the Notes column.
